      "title": "agent-infra/sandbox nginx auth bypass via query-string suffix allows unauthenticated file read and container-root RCE",
      "descriptions": [
        {
          "lang": "en",
          "value": "agent-infra/sandbox 1.11.0 selects its nginx auth workflow with a map keyed on \"$request_method:$request_uri\". Because $request_uri includes the query string, a GET request whose query ends in a static-asset extension (for example ?x=.json) matches the no-auth static-asset regex and is proxied by @proxy_without_auth, skipping auth_request. The aiod backend does not re-validate the API key. An unauthenticated network attacker can read files via /v1/file/download, open a shell WebSocket without an Authorization header, execute commands as the gem user, and escalate to root inside the container via passwordless sudo. The bypass is GET-only; POST endpoints still require authentication."
        }
      ],
      "affected": [
        {
